---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Tag from "../../components/ui/Tag.astro";

const stack = ["Computer Vision", "OpenCV", "Image Diffing", "Python"];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="This AI Compares Two Packaging Designs and Circles Exactly What Changed"
  description="A computer vision tool that compares two packaging design files and flags exactly what changed — built to catch the one edit a tired eye misses across thousands of near-identical revisions."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-28">
    <p class="label-mono mb-4">Minor project</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-medium tracking-tight">
      This AI Compares Two Packaging Designs and Circles Exactly What Changed
    </h1>

    <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted mt-6 leading-relaxed">
      Every packaging design at a company like Wings goes through dozens of revisions before it's approved for
      print — a price tag added, a net weight updated, a ribbon recolored. Someone has to hold the old proof next
      to the new one and catch every single change, by eye, across thousands of SKUs a year. Miss one, and it goes
      to print — which means a reprint at best, or the wrong number on a shelf at worst. I built a computer vision
      tool that compares two design files pixel by pixel and circles exactly what changed, so nothing depends on
      how sharp anyone's eyes still are on revision #400.
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 mt-6">
      {stack.map((t) => <Tag>{t}</Tag>)}
    </div>

    <p class="label-mono mt-16 mb-4">Can you spot it?</p>
    <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
      Below are two real design pairs — the kind that lands on a reviewer's desk every day. Take a few seconds and
      compare them yourself before revealing the answer. It's harder than it looks.
    </p>

    <!-- Example 1: Kopi -->
    <div class="mt-6 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-border bg-surface">
        <p class="label-mono text-ink-faint px-4 pt-3">Before</p>
        <img src="/demo/packaging-diff/kopi-before.jpg" alt="Original TOP Kopi Susu Gula packaging design proof" class="w-full h-auto mt-2" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-border bg-surface">
        <p class="label-mono text-ink-faint px-4 pt-3">After</p>
        <img src="/demo/packaging-diff/kopi-after.jpg" alt="Revised TOP Kopi Susu Gula packaging design proof" class="w-full h-auto mt-2" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <details class="mt-3 group">
      <summary class="label-mono cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center gap-2 text-accent">
        <span class="inline-block transition-transform group-open:rotate-90">›</span>
        Reveal what changed
      </summary>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-3 pl-5">
        A price tag — <span class="font-mono text-ink">"Harga Eceran Rp. 1.000 per sachet"</span> — was added to the
        empty gold box in the top-left corner. Everything else on the pack is untouched.
      </p>
    </details>

    <!-- Example 2: Sabun -->
    <div class="mt-10 space-y-3">
      <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-border bg-surface">
        <p class="label-mono text-ink-faint px-4 pt-3">Before</p>
        <img src="/demo/packaging-diff/sabun-before.jpg" alt="Original So Klin Softergent packaging print roll, five design lanes" class="w-full h-auto mt-2" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-border bg-surface">
        <p class="label-mono text-ink-faint px-4 pt-3">After</p>
        <img src="/demo/packaging-diff/sabun-after.jpg" alt="Revised So Klin Softergent packaging print roll, five design lanes" class="w-full h-auto mt-2" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <details class="mt-3 group">
      <summary class="label-mono cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center gap-2 text-accent">
        <span class="inline-block transition-transform group-open:rotate-90">›</span>
        Reveal what changed
      </summary>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mt-3 pl-5">
        The top tag was simplified from <span class="font-mono text-ink">"PACK JUMBO 42g Rp 1.000"</span> to <span class="font-mono text-ink">"PACK JUMBO Rp 1.000"</span> —
        and the net weight moved to a small badge in the corner, where it also quietly changed from <span class="font-mono text-ink">42g to 41g</span>.
        That second part is the one most people miss on a first pass — it's a real net-weight declaration, not just
        layout.
      </p>
    </details>

    <p class="label-mono mt-16 mb-6">Business impact</p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
        <p class="font-mono text-xl md:text-2xl font-medium text-accent">Pixel-exact</p>
        <p class="label-mono mt-1">Nothing too small to catch</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
        <p class="font-mono text-xl md:text-2xl font-medium text-accent">Seconds</p>
        <p class="label-mono mt-1">Not a full manual re-check</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface">
        <p class="font-mono text-xl md:text-2xl font-medium text-ink">No fatigue</p>
        <p class="label-mono mt-1">Same accuracy at #1 or #500</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-4 space-y-3">
      <div class="flex gap-4 p-4 rounded-xl border border-border border-l-4 border-l-accent bg-surface">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-accent-soft text-accent flex items-center justify-center">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="10" cy="10" r="6.5" />
            <line x1="15" y1="15" x2="20.5" y2="20.5" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">Catches what a tired eye skips.</span> Even a careful reviewer's
          accuracy drops after the twentieth near-identical proof in a row — a pixel-level diff doesn't get tired
          on revision #400.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4 p-4 rounded-xl border border-border border-l-4 border-l-warn bg-surface">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-warn-soft text-warn flex items-center justify-center">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M12 3 2 20h20L12 3Z" />
            <line x1="12" y1="10" x2="12" y2="14.5" />
            <circle cx="12" cy="17.3" r="0.6" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">Turns a compliance risk into a caught bug before print.</span> A
          missed net-weight change or price error that slips through isn't just embarrassing — it's a reprint, or
          the wrong number on a shelf. Catching it here is a lot cheaper than catching it in a store.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-4 p-4 rounded-xl border border-border border-l-4 border-l-accent bg-surface">
        <div class="shrink-0 w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-accent-soft text-accent flex items-center justify-center">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect x="3" y="3" width="8" height="8" rx="1.5" />
            <rect x="13" y="3" width="8" height="8" rx="1.5" />
            <rect x="3" y="13" width="8" height="8" rx="1.5" />
            <rect x="13" y="13" width="8" height="8" rx="1.5" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">Scales to the real volume, not just one comparison.</span> Built to
          run across a full batch of revisions — hundreds or thousands of design pairs — not just the one
          side-by-side someone remembers to run manually.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <details class="mt-16 group">
      <summary class="label-mono cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="inline-block transition-transform group-open:rotate-90">›</span>
        How it works (technical)
      </summary>
      <div class="text-ink-muted space-y-4 leading-relaxed mt-6 text-sm">
        <p>
          Two design files rarely line up pixel-for-pixel on their own — a rescan or re-export can shift or scale
          the artwork by a few pixels, which would swamp a naive diff with false positives. The pipeline first
          aligns the two images (feature matching + affine transform), then runs a structural difference pass
          rather than a raw pixel subtraction, so it's tolerant of compression noise but still sensitive to real
          content changes.
        </p>
        <p>
          The raw difference mask is cleaned up with morphological filtering to merge nearby changed pixels into
          coherent regions, then <span class="font-mono text-ink">cv2.findContours</span> extracts a bounding box
          around each one. Tiny, scattered differences below a size threshold are discarded as noise; everything
          else gets a box drawn around it and handed back to the reviewer — turning "compare these two images" into
          "look at these three highlighted spots."
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <p class="label-mono mt-16 mb-4">Data &amp; privacy</p>
    <div class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed p-4 rounded-xl border border-dashed border-border">
      <p>
        The packaging designs shown above are for real, publicly-sold retail products — the same artwork already
        printed on the pack you'd find on a store shelf. Internal production notes (print-run scheduling, target
        dates, printer/vendor names) that appeared on the original proof sheets have been cropped out before
        publishing here.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
